title: $:/TiddlyDesktop/Settings/Spellcheck
caption: Spellcheck
tags: $:/TiddlyDesktop/Settings

Spellcheck settings aren't available on Android. The desktop (NW.js) build drives Chromium's
own spellchecker through its browser profile — the local on/off switch, the dictionary language
and the opt-in for Google's remote spelling service all live there. This app uses the system
Android ~WebView, which has no such profile and leaves spelling to your keyboard, so none of
those settings would do anything here. This section is intentionally disabled.

Spelling suggestions, and the language they use, come from your ''keyboard'' (input method)
instead: change them in Android's own settings, where they apply to every app. There is no
remote-spellcheck opt-in to make here either — ~TiddlyDesktop sends nothing you type anywhere
on Android.
